        <headline>REPEAT ITEM TRACKING</headline>
        <description>Ref. HIL 55004534
  
 BACKGROUND: 
 An ACMS data review found a bleed spike (57psi LH, 51psi RH) that caused a RTO, and a small duct split during climb (43-45 psi on LH versus 40-45 psi on RH) and cruise (37-41 psi on LH versus 40-45 psi).
 NOTE 
 
 
 The aircraft is equipped with ACMS, no bleed sheets are required. 
 
  
 ACTION:  
 1. Obey safety precautions and get access to the engine#1 bleed components.  
  
 2. Use a pneumatic testing kit (P/N 1945-04-08) a do a complete pneumatic health check of the engine#1 bleed components. Refer to AMM 36-11-00.
 - Record the results and the S/N of the test kit you used on the RA851 form.
 NOTE 
 
 
 Send the RA851 form to bleedreview@ryanair.com. 
 
  
 3. Do a check of the engine#1 high stage regulator for a ruptured reverse-flow diaphragm.
  
 4. Do a detailed visual inspection of the engine#1 PRSOV for notchy behaviour, inability to remain open and actuator body leakage.
  
 5. Do a continuity check of the MW0311 harness as below:
 DP1104   ---   DP1102 Pin 12      ---   Pin 7 Pin 11      ---   Pin 6 Pin 3        ---   Pin 5 Pin 10      ---   Pin 10 Pin 2        ---   Pin 9
  
 6. If NFF, replace the High Stage Valve of engine#1. Refer to AMM 36-11-06-000-801 and 36-11-06-400-801.
  
 7. Record all findings in this workorder.
 - Make sure that you reinstate to a correct configuration all electrical (where applicable) and pneumatic fittings / components disturbed.
  
 8. Return the aircraft to service with all findings from this workorder documented and closed either through positive maintenance action or an acceptable deferral.</description>
